invariant: INV-16
file: src/p256_wide_field.h
catches: diff_p256_wide
reason: p256_wide_fe_half adds (p + 1) / 2 to the shifted words and drops
  the carry out of the third word. An odd element whose third shifted word
  has its top bit set, which is bit 0 of its fourth word, then halves to a
  value 2^192 too small. The differential halves p - 2, an odd element
  whose fourth word is odd, against the Lean product of it and the inverse
  of 2.

--- old
    o->word[3] = p256_wide_add_carry(&carry, s3, 0) + (half2 - half1);
--- new
    o->word[3] = s3 + (half2 - half1);
